course: dictionary
lesson: 7145
title: Peppercorn: a tiny berry with a big story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A peppercorn is a small dried berry from the pepper plant. When it is ground up, it makes the black or white pepper you shake onto your food. Cooks put whole peppercorns into stews, or crush them for a stronger taste.
explain: Peppercorns were once so valuable that people traded them across the world. Read this clue: «pepper was once so valuable it was used to pay rent». Something used to pay rent must be worth a lot, so pepper was a precious thing.
explain: Now read «a peppercorn rent». Here peppercorn does not mean a berry at all. The word rent sits next to it, and the rest of the phrase tells you it means something tiny, a token payment that is almost nothing.
explain: Space writers use peppercorns too. «If the Sun were a football, the Earth would be a peppercorn about 25 metres away.» Picture the huge Sun as a football and Earth as a speck next to it. The comparison tells you how small Earth is by comparison.
fact: A peppercorn is a small dried berry of the pepper plant.
fact: Black, white and green peppercorns are the same berry of a climbing vine from India.
fact: «Ground» peppercorns have been crushed into a powder, which is how pepper gets onto your dinner.
fact: A «peppercorn rent» is a tiny, almost free payment.
fact: The Sun is a gigantic ball of hot gas, and if it were a football, Earth would be a peppercorn about 25 metres away.
exercise: What is a peppercorn? | A grain of sand | A small metal coin | *A small dried berry of the pepper plant | A tiny fish that lives in rivers
exercise: «Pepper was once so valuable it was used to pay rent.» What does this tell you? | *Pepper was worth a lot | Rent was always paid in fish | Pepper only grows in gardens | Pepper was cheap and nobody wanted it
exercise: Nadia reads «a peppercorn rent» and asks what it means. Which answer is right? | A very big payment | A rent that goes up every year | A payment made in berries only | *A tiny, almost free payment
test: The Sun is a gigantic ball of hot gas. If the Sun were a football, what would Earth be? | A cloud | A star | A bigger football | *A peppercorn about 25 metres away
test: Which phrase uses peppercorn to mean a tiny payment? | *A peppercorn rent | Crushed peppercorns | Black peppercorns | Whole peppercorns
exam: Which two meanings does peppercorn have in this lesson? | *A dried berry and a tiny payment | A star and a planet | A grain of sand and a stone | A fish and a coin
